hat", "slot_byte_span": {"start": 117, "end": 128}, "boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0001", "MATHSEG_0002"], "classification_witness": {"usage": "root-phrase", "usage_source": {"before": ")\n", "after": "\ns", "environments": []}, "source_label": "categories-lemma-what-gets-inverted", "policy_hash": "sha256:6648093c080d9362cea0de2507eb65d250f9c12f8a00a7e5b534320688290537", "anchor": {"source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "file": "categories.tex", "owner_tag": "05Q9", "owner_label": "categories-lemma-what-gets-inverted", "kind": "lemma", "ordinal": 1, "matches": [{"container_byte_span": {"start": 171087, "end": 171628}, "container_hash": "sha256:4a04b32865ca9753948599563e73d7b9920ba514f52290377014e4495652a4b3", "command_byte_span": {"start": 171458, "end": 171476}, "command_hash": "sha256:f38c3a6f4a3ae96bb63f06d66d0263856c6151bb4c52d011527a027ab8bdf86b"}]}}}]}], "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:97fc3d224b52962a2581161fad4595c2fa23bd4c78c33e67afbbc22fcada440a", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d264bf8c8250eaf47fc60e7041dd9d4c3ee7c5b228aab147b2977ce71848f074", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:20ae5d2f40f458bfbb0611328693cead49d072f327b369012d25318b510538bb", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1847ed2fe4f48d89954e23fb961fff93765cd5d55864766cb569f04ead84635c"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:03NQ:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "03NQ", "chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThere is a canonical map\n<MATH_0001>,\n<MATH_0002>.\nWe say that a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>morphism of coverings<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> from a covering\n<MATH_0003> to <MATH_0004> is a triple\n<MATH_0005>, where\n<MATH_0006> is a morphism,\n<MATH_0007> is a map of sets, and for all\n<MATH_0008> the morphism <MATH_0009> fits into a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0010>\nGiven the data <MATH_0011> we define\n<MATH_0012>\nWe then claim that\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> the map is well-defined, and\n<STRUCT_0004> depends only on <MATH_0013> and is independent of the choice of\n<MATH_0014>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nWe omit the proof of the first fact.\nTo see part (2), consider another triple <MATH_0015> with\n<MATH_0016>. Then we have the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0017>\nGiven a section <MATH_0018>, its image in\n<MATH_0019> under the map given by\n<MATH_0020>\nis <MATH_0021>, and\nits image under the map given by <MATH_0022>\nis <MATH_0023>. These\ntwo are equal since by assumption <MATH_0024>\nand hence both are equal to the pullback of the common value\n<MATH_0025>\npulled back by the map <MATH_0026> in the diagram.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\check H^0 (\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0002": "$s \\mapsto (s |_{U_i})_{i\\in I}$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{V_j \\to V\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\chi, \\alpha, \\chi_j)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\chi : V \\to U$", "MATH_0007": "$\\alpha : J \\to I$", "MATH_0008": "$j \\in J$", "MATH_0009": "$\\chi_j$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nV_j \\ar[rr]_{\\chi_j} \\ar[d] & & U_{\\alpha(j)} \\ar[d] \\\\\nV \\ar[rr]^\\chi & & U.\n}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$\\chi, \\alpha, \\{\\chi_j\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0012": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\\check H^0(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{F}) & \\longrightarrow &\n\\check H^0(\\mathcal{V}, \\mathcal{F}) \\\\\n(s_i)_{i\\in I} & \\longmapsto &\n\\left(\\chi_j^*\\left(s_{\\alpha(j)}\\right)\\right)_{j\\in J}.\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "MATH_0013": "$\\chi$", "MATH_0014": "$\\alpha, \\{\\chi_j\\}_{j \\in J}$", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "MATH_0015": "$(\\psi, \\beta, \\psi_j)$", "MATH_0016": "$\\chi = \\psi$", "MATH_0017": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nV_j \\ar[rrr]_{(\\chi_j, \\psi_j)} \\ar[dd] & & &\nU_{\\alpha(j)} \\times_U U_{\\beta(j)} \\ar[dl] \\ar[dr] \\\\\n& & U_{\\alpha(j)} \\ar[dr] & &\nU_{\\beta(j)} \\ar[dl] \\\\\nV \\ar[rrr]^{\\chi = \\psi} & & & U.\n}\n$$", "MATH_0018": "$s \\in \\mathcal{F}(\\mathcal{U})$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{F}(V_j)$", "MATH_0020": "$(\\chi, \\alpha, \\{\\chi_j\\}_{j \\in J})$", "MATH_0021": "$\\chi_j^*s_{\\alpha(j)}$", "MATH_0022": "$(\\psi, \\beta, \\{\\psi_j\\}_{j \\in J})$", "MATH_0023": "$\\psi_j^*s_{\\beta(j)}$", "MATH_0024": "$s \\in \\check H^0(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0025": "$$\ns_{\\alpha(j)}|_{U_{\\alpha(j)} \\times_U U_{\\beta(j)}} =\ns_{\\beta(j)}|_{U_{\\alpha(j)} \\times_U U_{\\beta(j)}}\n$$", "MATH_0026": "$(\\chi_j, \\psi_j)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a13e04691eca3edbd05a9d84db375f884f9cfa46c11b85df2f91b013eae28d7", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3bb03ee421d41c779d6b4d21cf0588fea173444aea104c6c68cee956c35a2a3f", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a7dbdf79bda2d3598d6d6e5bf849923d8398ba9368fd3a533c2ede2b31a90fd6"}
